wifi: ath11k: do not read the 802.11 header of an encap offloaded frame

ath11k_dp_tx() tests the frame control of the frame for a 4-address
header. For a frame with IEEE80211_TX_CTL_HW_80211_ENCAP the first bytes
are the destination address, so the test misfires on addresses that
happen to look like a 4-address frame control. Skip it for encap
offloaded frames.

Signed-off-by: Julius Bairaktaris <julius@bairaktaris.de>

--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/dp_tx.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/dp_tx.c
@@ -213,7 +213,8 @@ tcl_ring_sel:
 		     FIELD_PREP(DP_TX_DESC_ID_POOL_ID, pool_id);
 	ti.encap_type = ath11k_dp_tx_get_encap_type(arvif, skb);
 
-	if (ieee80211_has_a4(hdr->frame_control) &&
+	if (!(info->flags & IEEE80211_TX_CTL_HW_80211_ENCAP) &&
+	    ieee80211_has_a4(hdr->frame_control) &&
 	    is_multicast_ether_addr(hdr->addr3) && arsta &&
 	    arsta->use_4addr_set) {
 		ti.meta_data_flags = arsta->tcl_metadata;
